From 0365f136ceb5aaa78dc4bfd1b77468c520362e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tkhs101 <tkhs101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:33:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] goodixtls: make the 27c6:5117 sensor usable end to end

Tested on an Honor MagicBook Pro 2020 (HLYL-WXX9) running firmware
GF_ST411SEC_APP_12118.

TLS transport:
- Port goodixtls.c from OpenSSL to GnuTLS. The GF511 sensors send a
  ClientHello without extensions, which OpenSSL rejects while GnuTLS
  accepts it. Restrict the priority to TLS 1.2 with PSK key exchange and
  AES-128-GCM, the only real suite the sensor offers (0x00a8).
- Read the TLS session key from /etc/goodix5117/psk (or $GOODIX_PSK_FILE)
  when present, falling back to the all-zero factory key. The 32 bytes
  returned by PRESET_PSK_READ (0xe4) are a digest of the white-box blob
  the Windows driver writes, not the TLS key.
- Feed each TLS record to the engine exactly once; calling
  gnutls_handshake() from two places fed the same record twice and made
  every step fail with "unexpected TLS handshake packet".
- Ignore the stray 0xd0 (request-TLS) packet that arrives around the
  handshake instead of failing the state machine on it.

Activation:
- Bring the TLS session up before the activation sequence. On 12118 the
  sensor boots straight into its TLS transport and only answers 0xae and
  0xd0 in clear text; everything else times out.
- Raise the image-capture timeout to 10s: the capture blocks until a
  finger is placed, so the 1s command budget is far too short.
- Accept any GF_ST411SEC_APP_* build; units ship different versions of
  the same firmware family.
- Warn instead of failing when the reported PSK digest differs from the
  factory value.
- Add an optional per-FDT-command MCU config hook.

Matching:
- Report finger-off right after a successful capture for non-enrol
  actions. Waiting for FTD_UP left the action pending until fprintd
  cancelled it, so a successful match was reported as verify-no-match.
- Do not report an error when the current action is already gone.

Debugging (environment-gated, no effect by default):
- GOODIX_DUMP_DIR dumps every captured frame as PGM.
- Log the residual dynamic range after calibration.
